<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yax Nuun Ayiin I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 404</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Curl Nose</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yax Nuun Ayiin I was a king of the Maya city of Tikal, installed as a boy in 379 after the arrival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyaj-kak">Siyaj K'ak'</a> and the death of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chak-tok-ichaak-i">Chak Tok Ich'aak I</a>. Inscriptions name his father as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spearthrower-owl">Spearthrower Owl</a>, possibly a ruler of Teotihuacan, and he is depicted in Teotihuacan-style dress and weapons. His son Siyaj Chan K'awiil II succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yax-nuun-ayiin-i.jpg" alt="Yax Nuun Ayiin I" width="320" height="558" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HJPD · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tikal_St04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
